course: dictionary
lesson: 2617
title: The little word des
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Des» is a tiny French word, not an English one. In French it means «some» before a plural noun, so «des pommes» is «some apples». Plural means more than one, so the little word in front tells you the thing comes in a group.
explain: «Des» can also mean «of the» or «from the» for plural things, as in «la maison des enfants», which means «the children's house». Notice that the little word in front does a lot of work: le means the one, les means the many, and des means some.
explain: You hear the plural in the little word, not the noun. «Le chat» sounds like "luh SHA", «les chats» sounds like "lay SHA", and «des chats» sounds like "day SHA", meaning «some cats». To an English ear, «des» sounds like "day".
fact: «Des» means «some» before a plural noun: «des pommes» means «some apples».
fact: «Des» can also mean «of the» or «from the» for plural things: «la maison des enfants» means «the children's house».
fact: After «pas», «des» becomes «de»: «J'ai des bonbons» but «Je n'ai pas de bonbons».
fact: Des is also a name, a short form of Desmond, and a familiar nickname in Ireland and the UK.
exercise: «J'ai des bonbons.» What does des mean here? | *some | from the | a single | the
exercise: «Je n'ai pas de bonbons.» Why has des changed to de? | Because bonbons is a name | Because it is a sad word | Because it means one | *Because it comes after pas
exercise: «Des pommes» means what in English? | the apples | some apple | an apple | *some apples
test: «La maison des enfants» means which English phrase? | the house of the cats | *the children's house | a big white house
test: How does «des chats» sound in English letters? | luh SHA | lay SHA | *day SHA | day sha-ah
exam: Des is a short form of which man's name? | Daniel | *Desmond | Derek | Dennis
